Interesting! In s05's opticon.c, the code is:

```c
const unsigned char *data = hdr + 2;
size_t data_len = urb->actual_length - 2;

if (urb->actual_length <= 2) {
    dev_dbg(...);
    return;
}
```

The check exists (actual_length <= 2), so the underflow is guarded — but note the subtraction `urb->actual_length - 2` happens BEFORE the check, but since data_len isn't used before the check returns, it's fine. Actually `urb->actual_length` is `u32` and data_len is size_t, so `urb->actual_length - 2` in C: u32 - int → u32 arithmetic, wraps mod 2^32 then converted to size_t... if actual_length==1, data_len = 0xFFFFFFFF, but then the check returns before use. So opticon.c in this tree is patched/safe. Good — this is the upstream fix (commit 7f7d8d1... actually the fix added the `if (urb->actual_length <= 2)` check).

So opticon is safe in s05. Now check kl5kusb105.c and greybus es2.c.

